  "city-gas-just-became-indias-largest-gas": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/CNG_filling_station%2C_Delhi.JPG/960px-CNG_filling_station%2C_Delhi.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"A CNG filling station in Delhi\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">City gas distribution &#8212; CNG for vehicles and PNG piped to kitchens &#8212; is the segment that overtook fertiliser plants as India&#8217;s top gas consumer. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CNG_filling_station,_Delhi.JPG\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CNG filling station, Delhi</a>, Subhashish Panigrahi, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
